# PostHog project token (public, safe for the browser) and ingest host.
# Copy to .env.local. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined at build time, so they
# must also be set in the deploy environment. Deployed, the token must be the
# one volcano-web's analytics uses in the same environment: visitors who
# accepted cookies on volcano.dev keep its stored PostHog id only when the
# tokens match (see src/lib/consented-analytics.mjs).
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# `true` turns on docs visitor analytics: visitors who accepted analytics
# cookies on volcano.dev get pageview analytics under volcano.dev's stored
# PostHog id (src/lib/consented-analytics.mjs); everyone else is counted
# anonymously, with nothing stored in the browser
# (src/lib/cookieless-counting.mjs), which needs the PostHog project's
# cookieless server hash mode or PostHog discards those events. Global Privacy
# Control turns both off. Unset or anything else leaves all of it off.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_COOKIELESS_COUNTING=
